[{"client_msg_id":"a6bf42f0-c144-4a01-ae77-3882b3b9a8b8","type":"message","user":"U03C4RC8X","text":"暑くなってきたのでだいぶ雪はslushyになってきました。しっかりグリップきくし転んでもあまり痛くないので良い感じです。:powderjou: ではないけど","ts":"1617079656.005800","team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"VPnp"}]},{"client_msg_id":"fe3b8352-d881-457c-9895-2e3c21779604","type":"message","user":"U03C4RC8X","text":"今日の様子です \u003chttps://vancouversnowboarding.wordpress.com/2021/03/29/2021-03-29-grouse-mountain-snow-report/\u003e","ts":"1617079591.004600","attachments":[{"fallback":"Vancouver Snowboarding Link: 2021-03-29 Grouse mountain snow\u0026nbsp;report","id":1,"author_name":"ujihisa","author_link":"https://vancouversnowboarding.wordpress.com/author/ujihisa/","title":"2021-03-29 Grouse mountain snow report","title_link":"https://vancouversnowboarding.wordpress.com/2021/03/29/2021-03-29-grouse-mountain-snow-report/","text":"Finally spring break is over. The first skyride in the morning is not 8am but 9am, and it\u0026rsquo;s still very busy.\n\n\n\nThe snow was hard packed in the morning but as the sun melts the ice under the snow the condition turned into slushy. It was stable enough to use the edges of your board anywhere but Expo.\n\n\n\nOverall rate: 4/5 \u0026#9733;\u0026#9733;\u0026#9733;\u0026#9733;\u0026#9734;\n\n\n\nClosed run:\n\n\n\nCoffin (Black)Closed chairlifts:\n\n\n\nPeak ChairOpen terrain parks:\n\n\n\nParadise Jib ParkCut Rookie ParkGrouse ParkThe Cut was greatThe CutPeak was great too. Not very icyView from the Peak was amazing tooIt was busy thoughI saw some people snowboarding on Hades and Inferno tooInfernoBlazes was great tooBlazes was harder at the lower section since the Blueberry Bowl was icier and bumpier, but still not badScreaming EagleGreenway chairBoth Screaming Eagle High-Speed Quad Chair and Olympic Express High-Speed Quad Char were very busy as a weekday standard","thumb_url":"https://vancouversnowboarding.files.wordpress.com/2021/03/blazes.jpg?fit=200%2C150","blocks":null,"service_name":"Vancouver Snowboarding","service_icon":"https://s2.wp.com/i/webclip.png","thumb_width":200,"thumb_height":105,"from_url":"https://vancouversnowboarding.wordpress.com/2021/03/29/2021-03-29-grouse-mountain-snow-report/","original_url":"https://vancouversnowboarding.wordpress.com/2021/03/29/2021-03-29-grouse-mountain-snow-report/"}],"team":"T03C4RC8V","replace_original":false,"delete_original":false,"blocks":[{"type":"rich_text","block_id":"g4yS"}]},{"type":"message","user":"U03C4RC8X","text":":flag--bc: なデザインにしました","ts":"1617079576.004200","files":[{"id":"F01TGBZM0HW","created":1617079568,"timestamp":1617079568,"name":"image.png","title":"image.png","mimetype":"image/png","image_exif_rotation":0,"filetype":"png","pretty_type":"PNG","user":"U03C4RC8X","mode":"hosted","editable":false,"is_external":false,"external_type":"","size":13199663,"url":"","url_download":"","url_private":"https://files.slack.com/files-pri/T03C4RC8V-F01TGBZM0HW/image.png","url_private_download":"https://files.slack.com/files-pri/T03C4RC8V-F01TGBZM0HW/download/image.png","original_h":2052,"original_w":2736,"thumb_64":"https://files.slack.com/files-tmb/T03C4RC8V-F01TGBZM0HW-fce0f18289/image_64.png","thumb_80":"https://files.slack.com/files-tmb/T03C4RC8V-F01TGBZM0HW-fce0f18289/image_80.png","thumb_160":"https://files.slack.com/files-tmb/T03C4RC8V-F01TGBZM0HW-fce0f18289/image_160.png","thumb_360":"https://files.slack.com/files-tmb/T03C4RC8V-F01TGBZM0HW-fce0f18289/image_360.png","thumb_360_gif":"","thumb_360_w":360,"thumb_360_h":270,"thumb_480":"https://files.slack.com/files-tmb/T03C4RC8V-F01TGBZM0HW-fce0f18289/image_480.png","thumb_480_w":480,"thumb_480_h":360,"thumb_720":"https://files.slack.com/files-tmb/T03C4RC8V-F01TGBZM0HW-fce0f18289/image_720.png","thumb_720_w":720,"thumb_720_h":540,"thumb_960":"https://files.slack.com/files-tmb/T03C4RC8V-F01TGBZM0HW-fce0f18289/image_960.png","thumb_960_w":960,"thumb_960_h":720,"thumb_1024":"htt